/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   ClearSky-OMEGA · TWIN FRAGMENT to firestore.rules
   © 2025–2026 ClearSky Energy Solutions LLC. Proprietary and Confidential.

   Backing store for the Tommy Twin service (clearskyenergy/omega-twin).
   Six collections, all prefixed `twin_`, all admin-only.

   HOW TO APPLY
   ─────────────
   This is NOT a complete rules file. It is ONE paste-in block: drop it
   anywhere inside `match /databases/{database}/documents`, alongside the
   C block of firestore.rules.control-plane.addendum. It defines no helper
   and touches no existing collection, so it cannot change the meaning of
   anything already deployed.

   Validate before pasting:
     node scripts/check-rules.js firestore.rules firestore-twin.rules
   That checks this block against the base file AS IF already merged —
   undefined helpers, same-scope duplicates, brace balance.

   Then search the LIVE rules text in the console for `twin_backlog`
   before calling it deployed. Same discipline as capacityAllocations:
   a rules file that fails to deploy leaves the previous version running
   and says nothing.

   ⚠ NOT DEPLOYED BY CLAUDE. Rules deploys are Tommy's, per CLAUDE.md §7.

   ── WHO THIS LETS IN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   isAdmin() is DOMAIN-based, not person-based: it is true for every
   clearsky-usa.com and csebuilders.com address, not for Tommy alone. That is
   the existing helper and the one the build plan names, so it is what this
   block uses — but understand what it is protecting. These six collections
   hold, in one place:

     · every meeting transcript the twin has ingested (twin_sources)
     · the 140-account sales pipeline with contacts and stages (twin_pipeline)
     · partner commitments to and from the OSA side (twin_meetings)
     · unsent email drafted in Tommy's voice (twin_drafts)

   That is the customer book plus the deal flow plus the JV's internal
   commitments. It is a strictly larger exposure than any single tenant
   collection in this file. If a ClearSky address is ever issued to a
   contractor, an intern, or a partner-side person, tighten this to a uid
   allowlist or an omega_staff role BEFORE that address is created — not
   after. Flagged, not fixed: narrowing it today would lock the twin's own
   admin surface out of its own data on day one.

   ── WHY THE SERVICE IS NOT MENTIONED ────────────────────────────────────────
   run-ingest, run-analyze, run-build and run-report all use the Firebase
   Admin SDK, which bypasses rules entirely. Nothing below is written for
   them. These rules exist for exactly one client: twin.html (Phase 3),
   where Tommy reads a brief and flips status on a phone. Read that as the
   scope of the whole block.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */


    /* ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       TWIN · the operating twin's state

       Six sibling collections, one grant. They are listed separately rather
       than folded into a single `match /{col}/{id}` with a prefix test,
       because a wildcard that matches on a NAME PATTERN would also match a
       future collection someone names twin_anything — including one holding
       data that should not inherit this grant by accident. Explicit is the
       point.

       sources   raw ingested email and transcripts, pre-parse
       meetings  parsed meetings: commitments split Tommy / others
       backlog   product items and their status through the approve gate
       pipeline  accounts, stages, next actions
       drafts    email awaiting Tommy's send. NEVER sent from the browser.
       runs      one doc per run: inputs, outputs, cost, errors, report text

       DELETE is granted. This is Tommy's own scratch state, not a tenant
       record and not an audit log with a retention obligation — the
       "flag, don't drop" rule in CLAUDE.md governs MIGRATION SCRIPTS over
       customer data, which this is not. twin_runs is the closest thing to a
       ledger here; if run history ever needs to survive Tommy's own thumb,
       drop delete on that one line and leave the other five.
       ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    match /twin_sources/{sourceId} {
      allow read, write: if isAdmin();
    }
    match /twin_meetings/{meetingId} {
      allow read, write: if isAdmin();
    }
    match /twin_backlog/{itemId} {
      allow read, write: if isAdmin();
    }
    match /twin_pipeline/{accountId} {
      allow read, write: if isAdmin();
    }
    match /twin_drafts/{draftId} {
      allow read, write: if isAdmin();
    }
    match /twin_runs/{runId} {
      allow read, write: if isAdmin();
    }
